 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? That depends on the paint. If it's oil, a week or so is ideal. If it's uv varnish, a couple of days is fine. That's still plenty of time. I'd wrap it in cling film and store in a cool dark place. It'll dry out perfectly. If you can't wait, you can use a hairdryer on the lowest setting and move it slowly. Just keep it away from your eyes. It' feel smooth and tacky, not sticky. If it still feels wet, give it some more time.",
